    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n108489" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑποκάμπτω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>bend short back,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὸ γλωχῖνα δ᾽ ἔκαμψαν</span> they
				<i>turned in</i> the strap-end <i>under</i> the strap
			itself, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				24.274
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑποκεκαμμένα [τὰ σκέλη</span>] <i><span class="en">
				Philum.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Aët.
				16.23
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> intr.,
				<i>turn back, double</i> as a hare, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyn.</u>
				5.16
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> metaph.,
			c. acc., <i>fall short of,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καιρὸν χάριτος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					786
				</span></i>
			 (anap.).</div>
